# The Complete Guide to Testing React Applications

Testing is the backbone of reliable software. A solid test suite catches bugs before users do, enables confident refactoring, and serves as living documentation. This guide covers everything you need to test React applications effectively.

## Why Testing Matters

- **Confidence**: Deploy without fear of breaking things
- **Refactoring Safety**: Change internals without changing behavior
- **Documentation**: Tests describe how code should work
- **Bug Prevention**: Catch regressions early
- **Collaboration**: New team members understand expected behavior

## The Testing Pyramid

```
        /  E2E  \         Few, slow, expensive
       /----------\       
      / Integration \     Moderate amount
     /----------------\
    /    Unit Tests    \   Many, fast, cheap
   /--------------------\
```

- **Unit Tests**: Test individual functions and components in isolation
- **Integration Tests**: Test how multiple components work together
- **E2E Tests**: Test complete user flows in a real browser

## Setting Up Jest

Jest is the most popular testing framework for React.

### Installation

```bash
# For Create React App - Jest is included!
# For Next.js
npm install --save-dev jest @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom
npm install --save-dev @testing-library/user-event

# Jest config for Next.js
npm install --save-dev jest-environment-jsdom
```

### Configuration

```javascript
// jest.config.js
const nextJest = require('next/jest');

const createJestConfig = nextJest({
  dir: './',
});

const config = {
  setupFilesAfterSetup: ['<rootDir>/jest.setup.js'],
  testEnvironment: 'jest-environment-jsdom',
  moduleNameMapper: {
    '^@/(.*)$': '<rootDir>/src/$1',
  },
};

module.exports = createJestConfig(config);
```

```javascript
// jest.setup.js
import '@testing-library/jest-dom';
```

## Unit Testing with Jest

### Testing Pure Functions

```javascript
// utils/format.js
export function formatPrice(cents) {
  return `$${(cents / 100).toFixed(2)}`;
}

export function slugify(text) {
  return text
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')
    .replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '');
}

// utils/format.test.js
import { formatPrice, slugify } from './format';

describe('formatPrice', () => {
  it('formats cents to dollar string', () => {
    expect(formatPrice(1999)).toBe('$19.99');
  });

  it('handles zero', () => {
    expect(formatPrice(0)).toBe('$0.00');
  });

  it('handles single digit cents', () => {
    expect(formatPrice(5)).toBe('$0.05');
  });
});

describe('slugify', () => {
  it('converts text to URL-friendly slug', () => {
    expect(slugify('Hello World')).toBe('hello-world');
  });

  it('removes special characters', () => {
    expect(slugify('React & Next.js!')).toBe('react-next-js');
  });

  it('trims leading/trailing dashes', () => {
    expect(slugify('  Hello  ')).toBe('hello');
  });
});
```

### Jest Matchers

```javascript
// Common matchers
expect(value).toBe(exact);           // Strict equality
expect(value).toEqual(object);       // Deep equality
expect(value).toBeTruthy();          // Truthy check
expect(value).toBeFalsy();           // Falsy check
expect(value).toBeNull();            // Null check
expect(value).toBeDefined();         // Defined check
expect(value).toContain(item);       // Array/string contains
expect(value).toHaveLength(n);       // Length check
expect(fn).toThrow();                // Throws error
expect(fn).toThrow('message');       // Throws specific error

// jest-dom matchers
expect(element).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(element).toBeVisible();
expect(element).toHaveTextContent('text');
expect(element).toBeDisabled();
expect(element).toHaveAttribute('href', '/about');
expect(element).toHaveClass('active');
```

### Mocking

```javascript
// Mock functions
const mockFn = jest.fn();
mockFn('hello');
expect(mockFn).toHaveBeenCalledWith('hello');
expect(mockFn).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);

// Mock return values
const mockFn = jest.fn()
  .mockReturnValueOnce('first')
  .mockReturnValueOnce('second')
  .mockReturnValue('default');

// Mock modules
jest.mock('./api', () => ({
  fetchUser: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({ name: 'John' }),
}));

// Mock with implementation
jest.mock('./analytics', () => ({
  track: jest.fn((event) => console.log(`Tracked: ${event}`)),
}));
```

## React Testing Library (RTL)

RTL encourages testing from the user's perspective.

### Core Philosophy

> "The more your tests resemble the way your software is used, the more confidence they can give you."

### Rendering Components

```javascript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import UserProfile from './UserProfile';

test('renders user name', () => {
  render(<UserProfile name="Jane Doe" email="jane@example.com" />);

  expect(screen.getByText('Jane Doe')).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText('jane@example.com')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

### Query Priority

RTL provides queries ordered by priority:

```javascript
// 1. Accessible by everyone
screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' });  // Best!
screen.getByLabelText('Email');                    // Form fields
screen.getByPlaceholderText('Search...');          // Fallback
screen.getByText('Welcome');                       // Visible text

// 2. Semantic queries
screen.getByAltText('Profile photo');              // Images
screen.getByTitle('Close');                        // Title attribute

// 3. Test IDs (last resort)
screen.getByTestId('custom-element');              // data-testid
```

### Query Variants

```javascript
// getBy - throws if not found (synchronous)
screen.getByText('Hello');         // Element must exist

// queryBy - returns null if not found (synchronous)
screen.queryByText('Hello');       // For asserting absence

// findBy - returns promise (asynchronous)
await screen.findByText('Hello');  // Waits for element

// getAllBy, queryAllBy, findAllBy - for multiple elements
screen.getAllByRole('listitem');
```

### User Interactions

```javascript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import LoginForm from './LoginForm';

test('submits login form', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  const handleSubmit = jest.fn();

  render(<LoginForm onSubmit={handleSubmit} />);

  // Type into fields
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Email'), 'jane@example.com');
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Password'), 'password123');

  // Click submit
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Log In' }));

  // Assert
  expect(handleSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
    email: 'jane@example.com',
    password: 'password123',
  });
});
```

### Testing Async Behavior

```javascript
import { render, screen, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import UserList from './UserList';

// Mock the API
jest.mock('./api', () => ({
  fetchUsers: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob' },
  ]),
}));

test('loads and displays users', async () => {
  render(<UserList />);

  // Loading state
  expect(screen.getByText('Loading...')).toBeInTheDocument();

  // Wait for data to load
  await screen.findByText('Alice');
  expect(screen.getByText('Bob')).toBeInTheDocument();

  // Loading should be gone
  expect(screen.queryByText('Loading...')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
});

test('displays error message on failure', async () => {
  const { fetchUsers } = require('./api');
  fetchUsers.mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('Network error'));

  render(<UserList />);

  await screen.findByText('Failed to load users');
});
```

### Testing Custom Hooks

```javascript
import { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';
import { useCounter } from './useCounter';

test('useCounter increments and decrements', () => {
  const { result } = renderHook(() => useCounter(0));

  expect(result.current.count).toBe(0);

  act(() => {
    result.current.increment();
  });

  expect(result.current.count).toBe(1);

  act(() => {
    result.current.decrement();
  });

  expect(result.current.count).toBe(0);
});
```

### Testing with Context

```javascript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ThemeProvider } from './ThemeContext';
import ThemedButton from './ThemedButton';

// Custom render with providers
function renderWithTheme(ui, { theme = 'light', ...options } = {}) {
  return render(
    <ThemeProvider value={theme}>{ui}</ThemeProvider>,
    options
  );
}

test('renders with dark theme', () => {
  renderWithTheme(<ThemedButton>Click me</ThemedButton>, {
    theme: 'dark',
  });

  expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toHaveClass('dark-theme');
});
```

## End-to-End Testing with Playwright

Playwright tests your app in real browsers.

### Setup

```bash
npm init playwright@latest
# Installs Playwright and browser binaries
```

### Configuration

```javascript
// playwright.config.js
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  testDir: './e2e',
  timeout: 30000,
  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
  use: {
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:3000',
    screenshot: 'only-on-failure',
    trace: 'on-first-retry',
  },
  webServer: {
    command: 'npm run dev',
    port: 3000,
    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,
  },
  projects: [
    { name: 'chromium', use: { browserName: 'chromium' } },
    { name: 'firefox', use: { browserName: 'firefox' } },
    { name: 'webkit', use: { browserName: 'webkit' } },
  ],
});
```

### Writing E2E Tests

```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('user can sign up and log in', async ({ page }) => {
  // Navigate to signup
  await page.goto('/signup');

  // Fill out the form
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('test@example.com');
  await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('SecurePass123!');
  await page.getByLabel('Confirm Password').fill('SecurePass123!');

  // Submit
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign Up' }).click();

  // Should redirect to dashboard
  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/dashboard');
  await expect(page.getByText('Welcome!')).toBeVisible();
});

test('user can create a new post', async ({ page }) => {
  // Login first
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('test@example.com');
  await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('SecurePass123!');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Log In' }).click();

  // Navigate to create post
  await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'New Post' }).click();

  // Fill out post form
  await page.getByLabel('Title').fill('My First Post');
  await page.getByLabel('Content').fill('This is a test post.');

  // Publish
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Publish' }).click();

  // Verify post appears
  await expect(page.getByText('My First Post')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.getByText('Published successfully')).toBeVisible();
});
```

### Page Object Model

```javascript
// e2e/pages/LoginPage.js
export class LoginPage {
  constructor(page) {
    this.page = page;
    this.emailInput = page.getByLabel('Email');
    this.passwordInput = page.getByLabel('Password');
    this.submitButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Log In' });
  }

  async goto() {
    await this.page.goto('/login');
  }

  async login(email, password) {
    await this.emailInput.fill(email);
    await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
    await this.submitButton.click();
  }
}

// e2e/tests/login.spec.js
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { LoginPage } from '../pages/LoginPage';

test('successful login', async ({ page }) => {
  const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);
  await loginPage.goto();
  await loginPage.login('user@example.com', 'password123');

  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/dashboard');
});
```

### Visual Regression Testing

```javascript
test('homepage matches screenshot', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/');

  // Full page screenshot comparison
  await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('homepage.png');

  // Element screenshot
  const header = page.locator('header');
  await expect(header).toHaveScreenshot('header.png');
});
```

### API Testing with Playwright

```javascript
test('API returns user data', async ({ request }) => {
  const response = await request.get('/api/users/1');

  expect(response.ok()).toBeTruthy();

  const user = await response.json();
  expect(user.name).toBe('John Doe');
  expect(user.email).toBeDefined();
});
```

## Testing Patterns & Best Practices

### Arrange-Act-Assert Pattern

```javascript
test('adds item to cart', async () => {
  // Arrange
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  render(<ProductPage product={mockProduct} />);

  // Act
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Add to Cart' }));

  // Assert
  expect(screen.getByText('1 item in cart')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

### What to Test

```
✅ DO Test:
- User interactions (clicks, typing, form submissions)
- Conditional rendering (loading states, errors, empty states)
- Component integration (data flow between components)
- Accessibility (roles, labels, focus management)
- Edge cases (empty data, very long text, special characters)

❌ DON'T Test:
- Implementation details (internal state, private methods)
- Third-party library internals
- CSS styles directly
- Exact DOM structure
```

### Test Organization

```
src/
  components/
    Button/
      Button.tsx
      Button.test.tsx      # Unit tests
  hooks/
    useAuth.ts
    useAuth.test.ts        # Hook tests
  utils/
    format.ts
    format.test.ts         # Utility tests
e2e/
  pages/
    LoginPage.ts           # Page objects
  tests/
    auth.spec.ts           # E2E tests
    checkout.spec.ts
```

## Testing Checklist

### Component Tests
1. Renders correctly with required props
2. Handles user interactions
3. Shows loading states
4. Displays error messages
5. Handles empty/edge cases
6. Accessibility (roles, labels)

### Integration Tests
1. Form submission flows
2. Data fetching and display
3. Navigation between pages
4. State management interactions

### E2E Tests
1. Critical user journeys (signup, login, checkout)
2. Cross-browser compatibility
3. Mobile responsiveness
4. Error recovery flows

## Conclusion

A comprehensive testing strategy combines unit, integration, and E2E tests to provide maximum confidence with reasonable maintenance cost.

**Key Takeaways:**
1. Test behavior, not implementation details
2. Use RTL queries by accessibility role first
3. Mock external dependencies, not internal modules
4. Write E2E tests for critical user journeys
5. Use the Page Object Model for maintainable E2E tests
6. Aim for confidence, not 100% coverage

Happy testing!
